cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Harara — anticipatory individualised heat-strain management for outdoor labour"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Muhammed Rasin
    family-names: "Bin Abdulla"
repository-code: "https://example.invalid/harara"
abstract: >
  Technical groundwork and two proof-of-concept contributions for
  forecast-driven, physiologically individualised heat-safety scheduling
  for Gulf outdoor workers: (1) a CVaR work/rest scheduler that beats the
  prevailing calendar rule, and (2) a physics-model particle filter for
  anticipatory individual core-temperature estimation.
keywords:
  - occupational heat stress
  - WBGT
  - thermoregulation
  - particle filter
  - stochastic scheduling
license: TBD
